From d36f3a43abf9c5bc0befcdf7627e5c6640822eda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cs16-arm <cs16-arm@local>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:27:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] arm: build for armv7-a / aarch64

- CMakeLists: no -m32/-msse3 on ARM, PIC for the shared object,
  arch-suffixed output (reunion_mm_armv7.so / reunion_mm_aarch64.so),
  -fpermissive on ARM only
- Rijndael / RijndaelChanged: S-box tables are explicit signed char.
  ARM's char is unsigned by default, so negative table initializers
  were brace-init narrowing errors (x86 behavior unchanged; all users
  mask & 0xFF or cast through unsigned char)
- dep rehlsdk: cpuid (sys_shared.cpp) and immintrin (crc32c.cpp)
  are x86-only, guarded out on ARM; osconfig.h drops x86 intrin
- reunion_authorizers: min(size_t, uint32_t) mixed types break
  aarch64 (size_t=unsigned long there); constants are size_t now
- pin reunion/version/appversion.h (gitignored upstream, but our
  build depends on it: appversion.sh wants a sibling ReHLDS checkout
  this tree doesn't carry)

see ReHLDS arm branch (same toolchain assumptions fanned out)
